msgid ""
"Install ROS by following the instructions on the ROS :doc:`Installation` "
"page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:53
msgid ""
"This guide assumes you have installed binary packages for your operating "
"system (deb packages on Linux). If you built ROS from source, you can still "
"follow this guide, but the path to your setup files is probably different."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:58
msgid ""
"If you installed from source, you cannot use ``sudo apt install ros-<distro>-"
"<package>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:60
msgid ""
"If you use Linux or macOS, but are not already familiar with the shell, "
"follow `this tutorial <https://www.linux.com/training-tutorials/bash-101-"
"working-cli/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:63
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:66
msgid "1 Source the setup files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:68
msgid ""
"Use the ``source`` command to import the environment variables which enable "
"your shell to access the ROS commands. You need to run this on every new "
"shell you open:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:73
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:105
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:150
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:196
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:243
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:303
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:75
msgid "$ source /opt/ros/rolling/setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:80
msgid ""
"If you're not using bash, replace ``.bash`` with one of the possible values: "
"``setup.bash``, ``setup.sh``, or ``setup.zsh``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:82
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:113
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:156
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:208
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:255
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:309
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:84
msgid "$ . ~/ros2_install/ros2-osx/setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:88
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:121
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:162
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:220
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:267
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:315
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:90
msgid "$ call C:\\dev\\ros2\\local_setup.bat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:95
msgid ""
"The exact command depends on where you installed ROS. If you have problems, "
"make sure that the file path leads to your installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:99
msgid "2 (Optional) Add sourcing to your shell startup script"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:101
msgid ""
"If you don't want to source the setup file every time you open a new shell, "
"you can add the following command to your shell startup script:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:107
msgid "$ echo \"source /opt/ros/rolling/setup.bash\" >> ~/.bashrc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:111
msgid ""
"To undo this, locate your system's shell startup script and remove the "
"``source`` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:115
msgid "$ echo \"source ~/ros2_install/ros2-osx/setup.bash\" >> ~/.bash_profile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:119
msgid ""
"To undo this, locate your system's shell startup script and remove the "
"appended ``source`` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:123
msgid ""
"If you use PowerShell, create a folder in **My Documents** named "
"**WindowsPowerShell**. Inside **WindowsPowerShell**, create the file "
"**Microsoft.PowerShell_profile.ps1**. Paste the following line into that "
"file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:127
msgid "$ C:\\dev\\ros2_rolling\\local_setup.ps1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:131
msgid ""
"PowerShell will request permission to run this script every time a new shell "
"is opened. To avoid that issue you can run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:134
msgid "$ Unblock-File C:\\dev\\ros2_rolling\\local_setup.ps1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:138
msgid "To undo this step, delete **Microsoft.PowerShell_profile.ps1**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:141
msgid "3 Check environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:143
msgid ""
"After you source the setup files, check that your shell picked up the ROS "
"environment variables. This confirms which distribution is active and "
"whether the ``source`` command succeeded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:146
msgid "To list ROS-related environment variables, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:152
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:158
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:305
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:311
msgid "$ printenv | grep -i ROS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:164
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:317
msgid "$ set | findstr -i ROS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:168
msgid ""
"Confirm that variables such as ``ROS_DISTRO`` and ``ROS_VERSION`` are set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:172
msgid ""
"ROS_VERSION=2\n"
"ROS_PYTHON_VERSION=3\n"
"ROS_DISTRO=rolling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:177
msgid ""
"If you later can't find or use packages, check these variables again and "
"make sure that they match the version and distribution you intended to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:179
msgid ""
"If the environment variables are not set correctly, return to the ROS "
"package installation section of the installation guide you followed. If you "
"need more specific help (because environment setup files can come from "
"different places), :doc:`get answers from the community <../The-ROS2-Project/"
"Contributing>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:183
msgid "3.1 (Optional) Set the ``ROS_DOMAIN_ID`` variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:185
msgid ""
"``ROS_DOMAIN_ID`` places your nodes in a DDS domain. Nodes only communicate "
"with other nodes in the same domain, so a unique value prevents your nodes "
"from seeing or being seen by other ROS nodes on the same network. For more "
"details, see the :doc:`domain ID <../ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Domain-ID>` "
"article."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:189
msgid ""
"For the value of ``ROS_DOMAIN_ID``, choose any integer between 0 and 101 "
"that no other ROS user on your network is using. If you are working alone or "
"on an isolated network, any value in that range is fine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:192
msgid "To set the ``ROS_DOMAIN_ID`` variable, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:198
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:210
msgid "$ export ROS_DOMAIN_ID=<your_domain_id>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:202
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:214
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:249
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:261
msgid ""
"To maintain this setting between shell sessions, you can add the command to "
"your shell startup script:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:204
msgid "$ echo \"export ROS_DOMAIN_ID=<your_domain_id>\" >> ~/.bashrc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:216
msgid "$ echo \"export ROS_DOMAIN_ID=<your_domain_id>\" >> ~/.bash_profile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:222
msgid "$ set ROS_DOMAIN_ID=<your_domain_id>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:226
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:273
msgid "If you want to make this permanent between shell sessions, also run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:228
msgid "$ setx ROS_DOMAIN_ID <your_domain_id>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:233
msgid "3.2 (Optional) Set the ``ROS_AUTOMATIC_DISCOVERY_RANGE`` variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:235
msgid ""
"By default, ROS nodes try to discover other nodes across the local network, "
"not only on your machine. The ``ROS_AUTOMATIC_DISCOVERY_RANGE`` environment "
"variable lets you limit how far that discovery reaches. This is helpful in "
"settings such as classrooms, where multiple robots may publish to the same "
"topic and interfere with one another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:239
msgid ""
"To limit discovery to the local machine, set the variable to ``LOCALHOST``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:245
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:257
msgid "$ export ROS_AUTOMATIC_DISCOVERY_RANGE=LOCALHOST"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:251
msgid "$ echo \"export ROS_AUTOMATIC_DISCOVERY_RANGE=LOCALHOST\" >> ~/.bashrc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:263
msgid ""
"$ echo \"export ROS_AUTOMATIC_DISCOVERY_RANGE=LOCALHOST\" >> ~/.bash_profile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:269
msgid "$ set ROS_AUTOMATIC_DISCOVERY_RANGE=LOCALHOST"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:275
msgid "$ setx ROS_AUTOMATIC_DISCOVERY_RANGE LOCALHOST"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment.rst:279
msgid ""
"For other values and more advanced discovery options, see :ref:`Improved "
"Dynamic Discovery <ImprovedDynamicDiscovery>`."
msgstr ""

